<title>USA: World Bank approves $20.9 mln loan for Georgia.</title>
<headline>World Bank approves $20.9 mln loan for Georgia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank said on Tuesday it approved a $20.9 million low-cost loan for Georgia to strengthen local governments there by helping to improve their management and financial base.</p>
<p>The project, financed by the Bank's International Development Association affiliate, aims to improve access to public services and help to raise living standards through investment in roads, lighting, schools and other measures, the lending agency said.</p>
<p>The 35-year loan to the former Soviet republic carries no interest charge.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
</text>
